5. SIMULTANEOUS OPERATION (solar at the window, a vehicle at 24 V, the full load, charging)
   the front end's input is the H3 line's at VIN_RAW whatever the sources share: at 24 V at most 4.194 A, 87.4 % of the entry's basis; the tracker's
   ceiling (28.28 V minimum) is above 24 V, so the panel carries the bus first and the vehicle supplies only what the panel does not give
   delivered at VBAT: 84.5 to 99.6 W (U3 between its minimum at the lowest bus and its board-current maximum at the bus's top, U3 0.9733)
   PS-IDLE-SPEC plan                    42.8 W: carried by the sources, up to 41.7 W left to charge (at most 3 A ChargeCurrent)
   PS-TYP plus USB-C plan              112.3 W: the pack supplies at least 27.8 W, 1.93 A at a 14.4 V stack; no charge
   the PA keyed alone at 113 W, plan   162.3 W: the pack supplies at least 77.8 W, 5.4 A at a 14.4 V stack; no charge
   PS-ALLTX plan                       203.8 W: the pack supplies at least 119.3 W, 8.28 A at a 14.4 V stack; no charge
   PS-ALLTX high                         272 W: the pack supplies at least 187.5 W, 13.02 A at a 14.4 V stack; no charge
   no stage is pushed past its limit: the entry stays under its minimum limit (H3), R11 carries at most 4.964 A, every can at most 2.4096 A, the pack's
   current falls by what the sources give (PS-ALLTX's floors of D-11 hold as on the pack alone), and the outlets drop while the PA keys
   per source at VBAT (U3 0.9733, VBUS20 20.96 V top, 19.146 V lowest): vehicle at 9 V 19.9 to 36.6 W (the entry itself bounds 9 V at 39.5 W); at 12 V up to 47.4 W; at 24 V up to 90.6 W
   so at the 9 V floor the vehicle runs PS-IDLE-SPEC (42.8 W) with the pack supplementing, and charges only while the kit draws under 19.9 W

6. STARTUP
   source arriving: the LM5069 starts at 9 V (UVLO, R21 '38.3k 1% (UVLO: 9 V)'), its timer bounds inrush; U3 is in HIZ below 8.466 V and out above 8.713 V; the H3 line
     bounds U3 from its first cycle with no host; the panel: the stage's own UVLO and soft start, the hold at 17.593 V
   source leaving: VBAT is the system node with no battery FET, so the pack carries the loads without a break; IIN_HOST resets to 3.25 A
     and firmware writes 4.7 A again (FW-A16 restated); VIN_RAW falls through the restart guard (8.31 V at the highest) and the front end stops
   dead pack (CUV opened the discharge FET): a source runs the loads through U3 at the pack's voltage while the charge clamps at 384 mA
     below VSYS_MIN; CONDITIONAL on TI's answer Q-TI-3 and O-CHG-2 (CHARGER-STATE-SEQUENCE.md); board E's always-on comes up on CELL_F from VBAT

7. FAULTS, TRACED ACROSS THE STAGES
   reversed vehicle input (REQ-015): DC_P is back-fed from VIN_RAW through Q7's body diode (L4-E5's finding), so Q1 holds DC_P plus the
     reversed input: 51.56 V with the drawn ceiling, 66.15 V with L4-E5's raised ceiling, against BSC039N06NS 60 V; a CSD19532Q5B (100 V) holds it,
     and U3's cathode to anode stays under its 70 V recommended and 75 V absolute
   a short behind F1: F1 must interrupt at up to 42.49 V (the OVLO maximum); the kit's cable (2 m of 1 mm2 a way) and lead (500 mm of AWG 18)
     give 0.0899 Ohm at 20 C and 0.0758 Ohm at -20 C, so a stiff source drives at most 560.7 A (copper alone); the held 297 is rated 32 V DC: NOT MET
   VBUS20 shorted: the front end holds the output at 4.57 A at 9 V (R12) and 7.262 A above 14 V (R11 8 mOhm); VIN_RAW then carries at most 11.65 A;
     the vehicle entry limits at 4.85 to 6.15 A and opens after 3.13 to 8.16 ms; the panel's stage limits at 3.4713 A; the restart guard cycles the front end
   VBAT shorted: the pack's SCD (60 A in 0.2 ms), OCD2, the 25 A blades and F2 against 240 to 480 A prospective; U3 at its input limit
   the pack's charge FET opening mid-charge (a designed event, REQ-046): VBAT is held at ChargeVoltage (16.884 V at most), BATOVP stops switching
     at 17.64 V, SYSOVP at 20 V; L2's energy at the stop, 0.1341 mJ (peak 6.896 A, L +20 %), into VBAT's 34 capacitors (248.2 uF nominal, 49.64 uF kept at 0.2)
     ends at 20.135 V from the SYSOVP maximum, under the TPS2596's 21 V; 6.54 uF would do (0.0264 of the nominal)
   U2 failed (Q2 short or FB open) and U3 lost: outside every requirement (ASM-001); s120 section 11 and S-111 carry the residual and the
     options (an SMCJ22A on VBUS20: VR 22 V over the 20.96 V band; an independent over-voltage trip)
   PoE monitor (HF-F02): U17's inputs at 54 V against the INA226's 40 V absolute: NOT MET as drawn; on a 20 mOhm shunt in the stage's VBAT
     input: 3.682 A at a 10 V stack, 73.64 mV against 81.92 mV full scale (at most 22.25 mOhm), common mode at most 20 V
   the solar entry's surge, a reversed panel and an LT8705A fault: PENDING: L4-E7R, the 100 W control decision on board E and the solar entry's surge protection (fnd/l4e7, fix round)

